"KV Cache Transform Coding for Compact Storage in LLM Inference (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.01815)\nciteturn4872academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Title: KV Cache Transform Coding for Compact Storage in LLM Inference ... Date: Mon Nov  3 18:20:35 2025\nTitle: KV Cache Transform Coding for Compact Storage in LLM Inference\nAuthors: Konrad Staniszewski, Adrian Łańcucki\nDate: Mon Nov  3 18:20:35 2025\n\nServing large language models (LLMs) at scale necessitates efficient key-value (KV) cache management. KV caches can be reused across conversation turns via shared-prefix prompts that are common in iterative code editing and chat. However, stale caches consume scarce GPU memory, require offloading, or force recomputation. We present KVTC, a lightweight transform coder that compresses KV caches for compact on-GPU and off-GPU storage. Drawing on classical media compression, KVTC combines PCA-based feature decorrelation, adaptive quantization, and entropy coding. It requires only a brief initial calibration and leaves model parameters unchanged. By exploiting redundancies in KV caches, KVTC achieves up to 20$\\times$ compression while maintaining reasoning and long-context accuracy, and 40$\\times$ or higher for specific use cases. We test KVTC with Llama 3, Mistral NeMo, and R1-Qwen 2.5 models across benchmarks including AIME25, LiveCodeBench, GSM8K, MMLU, Qasper, RULER, and MATH-500. It consistently outperforms inference-time baselines such as token eviction, quantization, and SVD-based methods, while achieving higher compression ratios. These results support KVTC as a practical building block for memory-efficient LLM serving with reusable KV caches.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPaper page - KV Cache Transform Coding for Compact Storage in LLM Inference (https://huggingface.co/papers/2511.01815)\nciteturn4872search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: last month; # KV Cache Transform Coding for Compact Storage in LLM InferencePublished on Nov 3, 2025\n\narxiv:2511.01815\n\nCopy markdown\n\n# KV Cache Transform Coding for Compact Storage in LLM Inference\n\nPublished on Nov 3, 2025\n\nUpvote 3\n\n  *   *   *   * Authors:\n\n[Button: Konrad Staniszewski] ,\n\n[Button: Adrian Łańcucki]\n\n## Abstract\n\nKVTC is a lightweight transform coder that compresses key-value caches for efficient large language model serving, achieving up to 20x compression while maintaining accuracy and outperforming existing methods.\n\nGenerated by Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct\n\nServing large language models (LLMs) at scale necessitates efficient key-value (KV) cache management. KV caches can be reused across conversation turns via shared-prefix prompts that are common in iterative code editing and chat. However, stale caches consume scarce GPU memory, require offloading, or force recomputation. We present KVTC, a lightweight transform coder that compresses KV caches for compact on-GPU and off-GPU storage. Drawing on classical media compression, KVTC combines PCA-based feature decorrelation, adaptive quantization, and entropy coding. It requires only a brief initial calibration and leaves model parameters unchanged. By exploiting redundancies in KV caches, KVTC achieves up to 20times compression while maintaining reasoning and long-context accuracy, and 40times or higher for specific use cases. We test KVTC with Llama 3, Mistral NeMo, and R1-Qwen 2.5 models across benchmarks including AIME25, LiveCodeBench, GSM8K, MMLU, Qasper, RULER, and MATH-500. It consistently outperforms inference-time baselines such as token eviction, quantization, and SVD-based methods, while achieving higher compression ratios. These results support KVTC as a practical building block for memory-efficient LLM serving with reusable KV caches.\n\nView arXiv page View PDF Add to collection--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKV Cache Transform Coding f